    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` to the spec. It keeps a per-client list of accepted `(time, cost)` entries and drops expired ones on each call. It checks the limit, window, cost and time-going-backwards rules and raises `ValueError` for each. `retry_after` returns a float. I wrote 22 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` covering invalid inputs, the exact-expiry boundary, rejected requests not using budget, client independence, costs and `retry_after`. They all pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I did not measure coverage, CRAP scores, mutation score or the bandit scan, so I can't say whether those gates pass.",
